# =============================================================================
# This repository is public. Treat every committed file as published.
#
# _build/ and _legacy/ are committed on purpose: _build/ is how the site is
# rebuilt, and _legacy/ is the previous version of the same public website.
#
# _private/ is working material that stays on the local machine. Three
# independent checks keep it that way, because the mistake is not reversible:
#   1. this file                      — keeps it out of `git add`
#   2. .git/hooks/pre-commit          — refuses the commit even if forced
#   3. _build/scripts/check-leaks.py  — fails the build if git can see it
#
# Guard 2 is not cloned with a repository. On a new machine, reinstall it:
#   bash _build/scripts/install-hooks.sh
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local-only working material. Never commit.
# Not in version control means NOT BACKED UP — keep a copy elsewhere.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
_private/

# OS clutter
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Editor and tool state — machine-specific, not part of the project
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
*.swp
*~

# Python bytecode from the build scripts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local scratch — anything here is disposable by definition
scratch/
tmp/
*.tmp
